    {
      "text": "prophet is not without honour, Matt. 13:57 (Mark 6:4; John 4:44). honour the Son, even as they honour the Father, John 5:23. I receive not honour from men, John 5:41. which receive honour one of another, and seek not the honour that cometh from God only, John 5:44. I honour my Father, and ye do dishonour me, John 8:49. honour myself, my honour is nothing: it is my Father that honoureth me, John 8:54. if any man serve me, him will my Father honour, John 12:26. Render therefore to all their dues … honour to whom honour, Rom. 13:7. Honour widows that are widows indeed, 1 Tim. 5:3. elders … be counted worthy of double honour, 1 Tim. 5:17. who hath builded the house hath more honour than the house, Heb. 3:3. no man taketh this honour unto himself, Heb. 5:4. honour and glory at the appearing of Jesus, 1 Pet. 1:7. Honour all men … Honour the king, 1 Pet. 2:17. honour unto the wife, as unto the weaker vessel, 1 Pet. 3:7. give honour to him: for the marriage of the Lamb, Rev. 19:7. kings … do bring their glory and honour, Rev. 21:24.",
